# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Personal-only files: anything built at your request that doesn't directly
# support the codebase (notes, drafts, one-off scripts, etc.). Never synced.
.personal/

# Zebra is an external validator run only as a benchmark/differential-testing
# oracle (CLAUDE.md Phase 0/2) — never part of zutreexo's own data. Its chain
# state defaults to a path outside this repo (see docker/.env); this is a
# fallback in case one ever lands under the repo root instead. See also
# docker/.gitignore, which excludes docker/.env and docker/state/.
/zebra/
/zebra-state/

# Phase 0 fixture corpus: ~65 MB of raw block hex per capture. The manifest is
# committed (fixtures/MANIFEST.sha256); the blocks themselves belong in LFS or
# a bucket, per CLAUDE.md Phase 0. Regenerate with scripts/measure_baseline.sh.
fixtures/*.jsonl

# ...except one. Every test that touches zutreexo-chain is gated on a fixture
# being present, so with all of them ignored CI executed *none* of that crate —
# block_apply.rs, extract.rs and pool.rs all measured 0.00% coverage, and the
# green checkmarks meant far less than they looked like.
#
# nu5-orchard is the smallest slice at 1.85 MB for 200 blocks (median block
# 2.2 KB). Committing just this one lifts workspace coverage from 74.50% to
# 92.50% — 18 of the 19.1 points that the full 65 MB corpus gives, for 2.8% of
# the bytes. The rest stay ignored: ironwood-activation alone is 59.3 MB because
# those blocks average 89.6 KB each.
#
# The other three slices still earn their place locally and in the nightly
# sweep, as differential-testing breadth — Sprout activity, sandblasting's
# pathological output counts, Ironwood — rather than as code coverage.
!fixtures/nu5-orchard.jsonl

# Personal drafts and notes — not project deliverables.
personal/

# Phase 5b run logs. The measurements they produce are transcribed into
# docs/benchmarks.md; the raw logs are machine- and night-specific.
/phase5b-runs/

# Coverage output. CI produces this with `cargo llvm-cov --json` and uploads it
# as a build artifact; scripts/check_coverage.py reads it in place. It is
# machine-specific and 1.7 MB, and it was committed once by accident.
/coverage.json
/coverage-ci.json

# Node PID files dropped in the repo root by local devnet scripts.
*.pid
